4tten deposits.\n\nA long-standing view holds that Anomalocaris fed on hard-bodied animals, making it one of the first predators\u2014and its raptorial frontal appendages mid-gut glands strongly suggest a predatory lifestyle.","price":null,"downloadCount":507,"editorUrl":"https:\/\/sketchfab.com\/models\/dad76e60589a41e18a42db1e979f81f8\/edit","status":{"warning":{},"processing":"SUCCEEDED"},"source":"website","hasCommentsDisabled":false,"updatedAt":"2022-06-21T23:46:12.040424","pbrType":"metalness","textureCount":6,"materialCount":1}